name c01m01-snake-eyes
timeout 700
time 1996-03-20T02:00:00Z

# F-22 LIGHTNING II (NovaLogic 1996), CAMPAIGN ONE "GAMBLING ON THE MEKONG", SORTIE 1.1 OF 8.
# Spec, provenance and every open question: mods/f22/doc/campaign.md, mods/f22/doc/terrain.md,
# mods/f22/doc/substitutions.md. Format: doc/missions/syntax.md.
#
# THE TASK [TXT]: establish air superiority over Chang Tzu Ming's MiG-27s. Flight group `Alpha` sits
# 50 NM NNW of FOB Tyler by the briefing, 54.3 NM on bearing 345.1 deg by the measurement [ORF].
# THE MEASUREMENT IS FLOWN, NOT THE PROSE — campaign.md 5 puts the briefed bearings up to 23.8 deg
# off, so the octant cannot place anything.
#
# ---- THE FIVE DISCLOSURES THAT APPLY TO ALL EIGHT FILES. Stated in full HERE; the other seven
# ---- carry the short form and point back at this file.
#
# D1  THERE IS NO F-22 IN THIS TREE AND NONE WAS INVENTED (CLAUDE.md, Prinzip 1). Storm Squadron flies
#     `module f16`. What that costs, in the direction of the error: no supercruise (Mach 1.58 [MAN
#     p.5]), no thrust vectoring, no +9 g (the F-16 limiter is +9 too, so this one is free), no reduced
#     signature at all — the F-16 is the LOUDER aircraft on every radar in the tree, so every detection
#     range against Storm Squadron here is an UPPER bound on what the real jet would have shown, and
#     every SAM engagement an upper bound on what it would have drawn. Stores map exactly where the
#     manual's do: AIM-120C -> `aim120`, AIM-9X -> `aim9`, M61A2 -> the F-16's M61A1. The magazine does
#     not: the manual states 480 rounds [MAN p.85] and `set gun_rounds 480` declares that number on an
#     airframe that holds 510.
#
# D2  CHAFF AND FLARES ARE NOT THE MANUAL'S. [MAN p.71-74] gives 100 chaff AND 100 flares. The F-16's
#     AN/ALE-47 holds 120 COMBINED (`FBF16Cmds::kMaxCombined`), and `set cmds_chaff 100` +
#     `set cmds_flare 100` is REFUSED at spawn with "chaff + flare exceeds 120 combined". Every file
#     therefore declares 60/60. That is not a tuning choice, it is the substitute airframe's dispenser,
#     and it means no F-22 mission in this campaign can measure the original's countermeasure DEPTH.
#
# D3  THE GROUND IS REAL AND MASKS NO DETECTION. `mods/f22/src/data/mekong-dem-90m.bin` is the
#     campaign box baked out of fb-tiles at Terrarium z13 onto a 90 m grid (data/README.md), named by
#     `mod.json`,
#     and `--elev baked` is therefore the default: every altitude in these eight files is ASL over the
#     real northern-Thai/Laotian surface, 97-2 547 m in the box, 271-1 485 m under the sorties. FOB
#     Tyler's reconstructed point is a 741.9 m hilltop; the raster answers 208.34 m at VTCN against a
#     published 209 m. WHAT THE GROUND STILL DOES NOT DO: exactly ONE sensor in the tree samples
#     terrain — `sensors/FBGroundMap`, the FCR's ground-MAPPING mode, which does compute grazing angle
#     and crest shadowing — and it writes a PICTURE (`FBGroundMapBlock` -> the MFD), never a detection.
#     No air-to-air radar mode, no IRST, no eye and no RWR has a terrain term at all, and no sortie
#     here selects `fcr_mode gm`. Measured: 1.1/1.4/1.6 fly byte-identically over real ground and over
#     the old plane, every detection and every miss distance to the digit. Terrain reaches these
#     sorties through exactly four doors: CFIT of aircraft, missiles and bombs; the launch ALTITUDE of
#     a ground site; AGL-driven pilot behaviour; and — in principle only, zero `horizon` events in
#     either run — the datalink's AGL radio horizon. Every detection range in this campaign is
#     therefore STILL an upper bound, and the reason is now a named engine gap, not a missing asset.
#
# D4  THE CLOCK'S DATE IS [SET] AND ITS TIME IS [DERIV]. campaign.md gives day-of-campaign and a local
#     hour, never a date. The base date is 1996-03-20, the EQUINOX, chosen because the sun's
#     declination is then ~0: at 19.4 N that puts sunrise and sunset within minutes of 0600/1800 local,
#     which is what makes campaign.md's own "1800 = dusk, 0230 and 0300 = night" come out true instead
#     of being asserted. A solstice date would bias every light number by up to +-23.4 deg of
#     declination. Local -> UTC is -7 h [DERIV, Indochina Time = UTC+7]. Day 1 = 1996-03-20, so
#     0900 local = 1996-03-20T02:00:00Z.
#
# D5  THE ANCHORING OF THE WHOLE BOX IS A RECONSTRUCTION WITH AN UNPROVEN ASSUMPTION (terrain.md 2).
#     One real anchor (Chiang Rai) plus "game +Z is geographic north", which eight compass octants
#     SUPPORT and cannot PROVE. If the map is rotated, every point in these eight files swings around
#     FOB Tyler by that angle — up to 50 km at sortie 1.8's range. The coordinates are terrain.md's,
#     recomputed here with terrain.md's own constants (111.32 km/deg lat) and reproducing its table.
#
# ---- THE SUBSTITUTION THIS FILE MAKES (full table: mods/f22/doc/substitutions.md)
#   MiG-27 Flogger-D -> `mig23` (MiG-23MLD). The MiG-27 IS the ground-attack Flogger: same swing-wing
#   airframe, same family. THE DIRECTION OF THE ERROR IS AGAINST THE PLAYER and is large: the real
#   MiG-27 carried NO air-intercept radar at all (a laser rangefinder in the nose), while the MLD row
#   in this tree sees 52 km, tracks 39 km, looks down 14 km head-on and shoots two R-24R. A bad Blue
#   result here therefore says LESS than it looks like it says.
#
# WHY 2 v 2 AND NOT MORE. Storm Squadron is the player plus ONE wingman [TXT], so Blue is fixed at two.
# Red is two because W1's saturation gate is a fixed point in this tree: an air-to-air result above two
# aircraft a side decides nothing (mods/f16/src/missions/w2-06-escort.fbm carries the argument).
#
# WHAT `Alpha` IS NOT: campaign.md's success condition is "Alpha destroyed AND all further hostile
# aircraft destroyed". There are no further hostile aircraft in this file, because the .ORF inventory
# for 1.1 adds NOTHING to the campaign's base set (campaign.md 4) — the second half of that condition
# has no object in the data and is therefore not declarable. Named, not silently dropped.
#
# READING RULE (binding). The verdict is `s1lead`'s UNIT_RESULT and nothing else.
#   SUCCESS/exit 0 requires all three of s1lead's objectives: `s1a1` dead, `s1a2` dead, and s1lead
#   still combat-effective when the run ends. Alpha down with one MiG alive is a MISSION LOSS, not an
#   engine defect, and reads as TIMEOUT/exit 3 with one `kill` unmet — do not report that as a bug.
#   exit 1 on `s1lead` = Storm Leader was shot: a mission loss.
#   exit 2 = a HOSTILE aircraft died that nobody declared, or an airframe departed controlled flight
#   with nobody having shot it. It is an ENGINE finding either way. It is NOT what a friendly loss
#   looks like: a friendly with `survive` fails DECISIVELY, which ends the run before its wreck can
#   reach the ground, and that reads exit 1 (measured four times over in this campaign).
#   `s1two`'s verdict is NOT the mission's: it carries `survive` alone so that its own loss stays
#   legible, and Storm Two dying while the leader completes is a damaged squadron, not a failed sortie.

# MEASURED (exit 3, real ground): ONE OF TWO. Storm fires ten rounds, brings one Flogger down and does
# not close the second.
#   t = 53.1 / 53.6 s   both leaders let an AIM-9 go first; eight AIM-120 follow between t = 66 and 398
#   t = 396.6 s         `s1a1` combat-ineffective; its wreck reaches the ground at t = 420.6 and ends
#                       the run (`FirstFlightKo`), which is why the sortie stops 279 s short of its
#                       own 700 s timeout
#   verdict             `s1lead` TIMEOUT — `kill unit s1a1` met, `kill unit s1a2` UNMET, `survive` met.
#                       `s1two` SUCCESS, `s1a2` alive
#   THE TERRAIN DELTA IS ONE NUMBER, AND IT IS THE PROOF BEHIND D3. Against the same sortie flown over
#   the old flat 0 m plane, every launch time, every DETONATION and every miss distance is IDENTICAL TO
#   THE DIGIT (4.57283 / 5.37654 / 5.07686 / 1.09741 / 4.98977 m). The ONLY thing that moved is when
#   `s1a1`'s wreck reached the ground: t = 422.5 -> 420.6, because the ground under 19.77 N / 99.98 E
#   is 428 m and not 0. An all-air sortie is therefore terrain-INVARIANT in this tree, which is what
#   "terrain masks no DETECTION" means when it is measured instead of asserted.
#   READ THIS AS A MISSION LOSS, exactly as the rule above says. Ten AIM-120 for one MiG-23 is the
#   number to report if anything here is to be reported as a defect, and it needs a second run before
#   it is one.

unit s1lead
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight storm1 1
  spawn 19.35656 100.20056 6000 345.1 450     # 40 km down-track of the Alpha point, co-altitude
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 1 aim9
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 7 aim120
  set store 8 aim120
  set store 9 aim9
  set gun_rounds 480                          # [MAN p.85], on a 510-round airframe (D1)
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60                           # D2: not the manual's 100
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 19.70380 100.10253 6000 450              # the Alpha point [ORF] 54.3 NM / 345.1 deg from Tyler
  wp 19.87742 100.05343 6000 450              # 20 km beyond it, so the vector does not end at the merge
  objective kill unit s1a1
  objective kill unit s1a2
  objective survive

unit s1two
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight storm1 2
  spawn 19.36002 100.21437 6000 345.1 450     # 1.5 km across track from the leader
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 1 aim9
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 7 aim120
  set store 8 aim120
  set store 9 aim9
  set gun_rounds 480
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 19.70380 100.10253 6000 450
  wp 19.87742 100.05343 6000 450
  objective survive

unit s1a1
  module mig23
  team hostile
  spawn 19.70380 100.10253 6000 165.1 450     # AT the measured Alpha point, inbound down the track
  set gear up
  set task intercept
  set brief_gci 165 40 6000                   # a controller's call, true bearing 165, 40 km, co-alt
  set store 1 r24r
  set store 2 r24r
  set brief_master_arm arm
  wp 19.18294 100.24950 6000 450
  objective survive

unit s1a2
  module mig23
  team hostile
  spawn 19.70033 100.08870 6000 165.1 450     # 1.5 km across track from its leader
  set gear up
  set task intercept
  set brief_gci 165 40 6000
  set store 1 r24r
  set store 2 r24r
  set brief_master_arm arm
  wp 19.18294 100.24950 6000 450
  objective survive
